# Continue Implementation: System-Wide Protocol

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines the protocol for continuing a system-wide implementation within the rules-workflow. It should be used when:

- Continuing implementation of system-wide changes
- Resuming a system-wide implementation after interruption
- Maintaining implementation momentum across multiple system components
- Restoring context for large-scale system modifications

This protocol ensures consistent handling of system-wide implementations.

## Project Rule Parameter

Loyal to: continue-implementation: @parameters/rules/continue-implementation-system-wide.mdc

## Call Pattern

Message-Command: continue-implementation
Standard-Parameters: none
Example: `continue-implementation: @continue-implementation-system-wide.mdc`

## Relation to Cognitive Architecture

This file is part of the rules-workflow knowledge component within the 1000xbrain cognitive architecture. It complements:

- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/patterns/impl/implementation-patterns"])`: System-wide implementation patterns
- `@parameters/rules/dev-mode-system-wide.mdc`: System-wide development protocol
- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/reference/guides/implementation-patterns"])`: Implementation status checking
- `fetch_rules(["knowledge/reference/guides/knowledge-system"])`: System-wide planning protocol

